implementationPlan.description:
1. Protect the board boundary with tests first (DoD 1). After WT-03 lands, use its real LandingRetry type/shape in the existing /ws harness; no `any` stand-in or schema edit. Add a compact parameterized test beside the UPDATE_TASK evidence-strip tests covering stored retry + incoming forged object, stored retry + incoming null, and stored null + incoming stale retry object. Seed before installing spies; send each mixed update with an allowed title change using connectAndCollect and consume STATE_SNAPSHOT. Assert title applied in the TASK_UPDATED response and state, stored/disk landingRetry equals its pre-request value, and the retry object is never passed into state.updateTask at all (spy on forwarded updates, not only the final state). For example:
```ts
const update = vi.spyOn(state, 'updateTask');
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'UPDATE_TASK', payload: { taskId: 'task-1', updates: { title: 'Allowed edit', landingRetry: forged } } }));
await nextTaskUpdated(nextMessage);
expect(update.mock.calls.find(([id]) => id === 'task-1')?.[1]).not.toHaveProperty('landingRetry');
expect(state.getTask('task-1')?.landingRetry).toEqual(stored);
```
Close socket/restore spy in finally. Add only `'landingRetry'` to UPDATE_TASK_DENYLIST with a short comment that finalize_attempt owns it and board echoes cannot restore/clear/forge it. Retain existing stripping behavior, not whole-message rejection, so allowed fields still apply. Existing invalid-envelope/error handling must remain unchanged.

2. Keep unlanded retries claimable by workers, with tests first (DoD 2). In releaseTask.test.ts reuse writeTask/writeWorker/state fixtures. Parameterize real releaseTaskTool.handler calls for WORKING tasks whose nonempty plan is all COMPLETED: non-null landingRetry => WORKING/unassigned; null and omitted landingRetry => REVIEW/unassigned. Cover both an assigned worker-a and the already-unassigned repair path; assert retry metadata and completed steps persist unchanged in memory and task JSON, and the assigned worker is freed/IDLE where applicable. Use a valid producer-shaped retry, e.g. reason conflict, paths ['src/a.ts'], rescueRef 'refs/moe/rescue/task-1/20261030T120000Z', targetTip null, count 1, valid ISO at. Also exercise exported releaseWorkerTasks(state,'worker-a','test park','park') on a retry task and assert BACKLOG/unassigned with retry metadata intact. Preserve existing incomplete-plan, terminal, missing-task and release-failure tests. Implement the minimal shared rule:
```ts
// nextStatusForRelease parameter:
task: Pick<Task, 'status' | 'implementationPlan' | 'landingRetry'>
// WORKING case, after existing park early return:
if (task.landingRetry != null) return 'WORKING';
return allStepsCompleted(task) ? 'REVIEW' : 'WORKING';
```
Update this function's local routing comment to explain the retry exception. Verify all current callers in workerStore.ts, sweeps.ts, taskStore.ts, releaseTask.ts, unblockWorker.ts and releaseWorkerTasks pass the full Task; these are read-only inspection paths, not additional edits. Do not alter BLOCKED/REVIEW/terminal routing, clear retry data, reopen steps, change counters, or duplicate logic at individual release callers.
